    thinkr:dataSourceCitation "1) World Meteorological Organization (WMO). (2022). Scientific Assessment of Ozone Depletion: 2022, GAW Report No. 278, 509 pp. 2) Richardson, K., et al. (2023). Earth beyond six of nine planetary boundaries. Sci. Adv.9, eadh2458." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Definition and value from the California Doughnut Snapshot (pp. 9-12), updated 2026-10-23; the value is the report's percentage overshoot beyond the ecological ceiling. Earlier paraphrased definition: 'The density and health of stratospheric ozone, which filters out cancer-causing ultraviolet (UV) rays.' Not in overshoot: Ozone Depletion is the only ecological category within its ceiling. Value, threshold, years and sources from CalDEC's companion indicator sheet (tgs:Work.CaliforniaDoughnutIndicators2025), added 2026-10-23; the gap now uses the sheet's unrounded figure. Measured 284 Dobson units, about 3% above the boundary, so not in overshoot; recorded as 0."@en .

